  <h2>Conclusion</h2>

  <p>The Pomodoro Technique is not magic — it is structured common sense grounded in how human attention actually functions. By dividing work into manageable intervals and honouring breaks, you train your brain to focus on demand. It works because it respects your biological rhythms, not because it imposes arbitrary discipline.</p>

  <p>Try it for one day. Set a timer for 25 minutes, pick one task, and work until it rings. Then take your break. Repeat. You may be surprised how much you accomplish.</p>

